---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import Card from '../../components/ui/Card.astro';
import CardContent from '../../components/ui/CardContent.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';

const headings = [
  { text: "Overview", slug: "overview", depth: 2 },
  { text: "Public Status Page", slug: "public-status-page", depth: 2 },
  { text: "Email Subscriptions", slug: "email-subscriptions", depth: 2 },
  { text: "Subscribing", slug: "subscribing", depth: 2 },
  { text: "What Subscribers Receive", slug: "what-subscribers-receive", depth: 2 },
  { text: "Unsubscribing", slug: "unsubscribing", depth: 2 },
  { text: "Managing Subscribers", slug: "managing-subscribers", depth: 2 },
  { text: "Limits", slug: "limits", depth: 2 },
  { text: "API", slug: "api", depth: 2 }
];

const keywords = [
  "LogTide status page",
  "status page email subscriptions",
  "status page double opt-in",
  "uptime status page subscribers",
  "self-hosted status page"
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Status Page Subscriptions"
  description="The LogTide public status page and its email subscriptions: double opt-in, the updates subscribers receive, one-click unsubscribe, managing subscribers, and limits."
  keywords={keywords}
  headings={headings}
>
  <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
    <div class="p-2 bg-primary/10 rounded-lg">
      <Icon name="lucide:mail-check" class="w-6 h-6 text-primary-readable" />
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Status Page Subscriptions</h1>
  </div>

  <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground mb-8">
    Let your users subscribe by email to your public status page. They confirm their address once
    and then hear about status updates and scheduled maintenance without checking the page.
  </p>

  <h2 id="overview" class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 scroll-mt-24 border-b border-border pb-2">
    Overview
  </h2>

  <div class="mb-8 space-y-4">
    <p>
      Subscriptions are offered only when both of these are true, otherwise the subscribe form is
      hidden and the subscribe endpoint answers 404:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-2">
      <li>the project's status page visibility is <strong>Public</strong> (not password protected, members only or disabled), and</li>
      <li>SMTP is configured on the LogTide instance.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2 id="public-status-page" class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 scroll-mt-24 border-b border-border pb-2">
    Public Status Page
  </h2>

  <div class="mb-8 space-y-4">
    <p>
      Each project has its own page at <code>/status/&lt;organization-slug&gt;/&lt;project-slug&gt;</code>.
      It shows the current state of the project's monitors, ongoing and past
      <strong>status updates</strong> (the public communications about incidents, written by your
      team) and scheduled maintenance. Owners and admins can set the page title, description, logo
      URL and accent color, choose which monitors appear as components with a public display
      name, group and order, and show monitor types. Visibility is a project setting: public,
      password protected, members only or disabled.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      Status updates are separate from the internal <a href="/docs/incidents/">incidents inbox</a>.
      You can publish an uptime incident to the status page as a pre-filled status update.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="email-subscriptions" class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 scroll-mt-24 border-b border-border pb-2">
    Email Subscriptions
  </h2>

  <div class="mb-8 space-y-4">
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <Card>
        <CardContent class="pt-4">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <Icon name="lucide:shield-check" class="w-5 h-5 text-primary-readable mt-0.5 shrink-0" />
            <div>
              <h4 class="font-medium mb-1">Double opt-in</h4>
              <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">An address receives updates only after its owner clicks the link in a confirmation email.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>

      <Card>
        <CardContent class="pt-4">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <Icon name="lucide:mouse-pointer-click" class="w-5 h-5 text-primary-readable mt-0.5 shrink-0" />
            <div>
              <h4 class="font-medium mb-1">One-click unsubscribe</h4>
              <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Every update email carries a signed unsubscribe link. No account or password involved.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="subscribing" class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 scroll-mt-24 border-b border-border pb-2">
    Subscribing
  </h2>

  <div class="mb-8 space-y-4">
    <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 ml-2">
      <li>A visitor enters an email address in the subscribe form on the public page.</li>
      <li>LogTide sends a confirmation email with a link that is valid for 48 hours and can be used once.</li>
      <li>Opening the link activates the subscription.</li>
    </ol>

    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-2">
      <li>The page answers the same way whether or not the address is already known, so the form cannot be used to find out who is subscribed.</li>
      <li>Submitting an address that is still waiting for confirmation sends a fresh link, at most once per minute and at most 3 confirmation emails per address in 24 hours. An address that is already confirmed is left alone.</li>
      <li>Each status page keeps at most 200 unconfirmed addresses. Beyond that, new addresses are silently ignored until old links expire.</li>
      <li>Addresses that never confirm expire with their link and never count against your subscriber limit.</li>
      <li>Confirmation and unsubscribe links open a status page that completes the action itself with a <code>POST</code> request, so a mail scanner that only fetches the URL does not subscribe or unsubscribe anyone.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2 id="what-subscribers-receive" class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 scroll-mt-24 border-b border-border pb-2">
    What Subscribers Receive
  </h2>

  <div class="mb-8 space-y-4">
    <p>Confirmed subscribers of a page are emailed when:</p>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-border text-left">
            <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Event</th>
            <th class="py-2 font-semibold">Email heading</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-muted-foreground">
          <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4">A status update is created</td><td class="py-2">New incident</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4">A status update gets a new message</td><td class="py-2">Incident update</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4">A status update is resolved</td><td class="py-2">Incident resolved</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">Scheduled maintenance is created</td><td class="py-2">Scheduled maintenance, with its start and end time</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      The subject line starts with the page title, for example
      <code>[Acme Status] Resolved: Checkout errors</code>. Internal incidents, alerts and monitor
      checks never email subscribers; only the status updates and maintenance you publish do.
      Nothing is sent if the page has stopped being public or SMTP is no longer configured.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="unsubscribing" class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 scroll-mt-24 border-b border-border pb-2">
    Unsubscribing
  </h2>

  <div class="mb-8 space-y-4">
    <p>
      Each email ends with an <strong>Unsubscribe</strong> link. The link holds a token signed with
      your instance's <code>API_KEY_SECRET</code>, so it needs no stored secret per subscriber and
      cannot be forged. Unsubscribing removes the address immediately. The link keeps working even
      if the page is no longer public, so nobody gets stuck on your list. Rotating
      <code>API_KEY_SECRET</code> invalidates links in emails already sent.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="managing-subscribers" class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 scroll-mt-24 border-b border-border pb-2">
    Managing Subscribers
  </h2>

  <div class="mb-8 space-y-4">
    <p>
      In the status page settings, organization owners and admins can see the confirmed
      subscribers of a page (50 per page, newest first) and remove any of them. Members cannot
      see subscriber addresses. Changes to the status page configuration, components and
      subscribers are recorded in the audit log.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="limits" class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 scroll-mt-24 border-b border-border pb-2">
    Limits
  </h2>

  <div class="mb-8 space-y-4">
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-border text-left">
            <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Limit</th>
            <th class="py-2 font-semibold">Value</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-muted-foreground">
          <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Subscribers per organization</td><td class="py-2">Unlimited by default. Set the <code>status_page.subscribers.max</code> capability to cap it. Only confirmed subscribers count. At the cap, no new confirmation emails are sent and confirmation links stop working.</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Subscribe requests</td><td class="py-2">5 per minute per client address</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Confirmation link lifetime</td><td class="py-2">48 hours, single use</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Confirmation emails for the same address</td><td class="py-2">At most one per minute and 3 per 24 hours</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Unconfirmed addresses per status page</td><td class="py-2">200</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">Email address length</td><td class="py-2">254 characters</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="api" class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 scroll-mt-24 border-b border-border pb-2">
    API
  </h2>

  <div class="mb-8 space-y-4">
    <p>
      The public endpoints need no authentication. They are what the status page itself calls.
    </p>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-border text-left">
            <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Endpoint</th>
            <th class="py-2 font-semibold">Purpose</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-muted-foreground">
          <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>POST /api/v1/status/:orgSlug/:projectSlug/subscribe</code></td><td class="py-2">Body <code>{`{ "email": "..." }`}</code>. Answers 202 whether or not the address is known, new, rate limited or over a limit.</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>POST /api/v1/status/:orgSlug/:projectSlug/subscribe/confirm</code></td><td class="py-2">Body <code>{`{ "token": "..." }`}</code>. 400 for an unknown, expired or used link.</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>POST /api/v1/status/:orgSlug/:projectSlug/unsubscribe</code></td><td class="py-2">Body <code>{`{ "token": "..." }`}</code>. 400 for an invalid link.</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>GET /api/v1/status-page/subscribers</code></td><td class="py-2">Signed-in owners and admins: confirmed subscribers of a project (<code>organizationId</code>, <code>projectId</code>, <code>page</code>).</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>DELETE /api/v1/status-page/subscribers/:id</code></td><td class="py-2">Signed-in owners and admins: remove a subscriber.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <Code
      lang="bash"
      theme="one-dark-pro"
      code={`curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/status/acme/api/subscribe \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{ "email": "oncall@example.com" }'`}
    />
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
